The Hellenistic Philosophers — Long and Sedley (@greek-source-long-sedley: 0, is #book, #part-of @greek-scholarly-sources) { r_0DRQW2CEH35TV91C49W4JH7Y0M
A. A. Long and D. N. Sedley. The Hellenistic Philosophers. Cambridge University Press, 1987, two volumes. Volume I: translations of the principal sources with philosophical commentary. Volume II: Greek and Latin texts with notes and bibliography.

[Publisher's volume II record and relation to volume I](https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/the-hellenistic-philosophers/A11641C811C80041E4B1DAE059C3D8AE).

Use both sides of the collection for [the Hellenistic seminar](../research/seminars/Hellenistic-disputes.lingua#r_7020B909F5EN8WYCK7HZ0F1ZBV): the arguments and their source-language evidence. Follow selected testimonies back to the surviving context and identify dependencies between reports.

**Access:** publisher, library, or owned volumes. The collection supports a thematic investigation and a literature search; read later work relevant to the chosen debate.
